  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through Wednesday)\nIssued at 1207 AM CDT Thu May 28 2026\n\nAn unsettled weather pattern will persist through much of the \nlong term with a persistent weak upper level west-southwest flow \nwith disturbances moving across our area mainly Friday night \nthrough Monday. Also, a surface dryline will be located to our \nwest late this weekend and early next week. There will be moderate\ninstability and abundant moisture in the area but lift will be \nweak through the long term. The severe weather chances look low at\nthis time, but can not rule out an isolated strong to marginal \nsevere storm, especially Friday evening across northern and \nwestern areas as convection moving in from the west will be \nweakening. Going with mainly low chances of rain through much of \nthe long term, mainly isolated to widely scattered afternoon and \nevening showers and thunderstorms. Most areas will see little \nrainfall through the long term. Expect a slow warming trend with \nhighs in the upper 80s to upper 90s by this weekend, cooling back \ninto the 80s by the middle of next week.",
